{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - 1.\tThe proposed front boundary treatment, by reason of its height and design, together with the number of rooflights and in the absence of sufficient information to demonstrate that the replacement of the render with brick slips and specific window details would preserve the character and appearance of the dwelling and wider conservation area, the development would be contrary to policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC4 (Heritage), SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations) of the adopted Local Plan (2015) and the intentions of the Residential Extension Guidelines of the adopted Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD (Part A5) and the Conservation Area Appraisal for St Stephens Conservation Area",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed off-street parking space within the forecourt of the house, on account of existing site constraints and proposed orientation, would fail to comply with the minimum requirements of the Residential Crossovers and Off-Street Parking Policy, Local Plan policy EC2 and would therefore be detrimental to highway and pedestrian safety and would lead to the loss of greenery within the front garden which would be contrary to the aims and objectives of the Conservation Area Appraisal for St Stephens Conservation Area and Local Plan policy CC4."
  ],
